# nr-office-ooxml-pptx-shapes: integration fragment

New module `pptx_shapes` of the crate mixdog-ooxml: the shape operations of `portable/portable-pptx-shapes.mjs`
(set_hyperlink, z_order, align_shapes / distribute_shapes, set_text, add_textbox / add_shape, delete_shape, add_table,
add_image, fit_text, set_table_cell_style, set_table_data / replace_image, group_shapes / ungroup_shape, add_media,
crop_image, add_animation, set_shape). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to it.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

Add the module declaration (beside `pub mod pptx_package;`, keep the other tasks' lines):

    pub mod pptx_shapes;

## Dependencies

None. The module uses mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, serde_json and the modules of the crate that are already
dependencies of mixdog-ooxml; the twin test uses base64, tempfile, mixdog-fonts and mixdog-office-base (feature
test-support), all already in its Cargo.toml. native/core/Cargo.lock does not change.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-pptx-deck (or office-pptx-base when the deck set is not listed yet; keep the list
sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-shapes.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-pptx-shapes/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "9bd288ea562ace1e63d225c572cef48f08ea47698d1dcd3d5ca28a41239abe59",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-shapes.mjs",
      "set": "office-pptx-shapes",
      "totalBytes": 255076
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-pptx-shapes/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that
keeps this file reorders or reformats them: `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index`.)

## For the task that ports `portable-pptx.mjs` (the operation dispatcher)

The handlers take the package, the slides the presentation lists (`presentation_slides(zip)`, recomputed after the operations
that renumber slides, as Node's context does) and the operation as a `serde_json::Value`; they answer `Result<Value, String>`
(the JSON the script returned, or the message of the error it threw). Where Node's table named one handler for two operations
the Rust function keeps that name and reads `op.op`:

    set_hyperlink                          pptx_shapes::set_hyperlink(zip, slides, op)
    z_order                                pptx_shapes::z_order(zip, slides, op)
    align_shapes, distribute_shapes        pptx_shapes::align_shapes_or_distribute_shapes(zip, slides, op)
    set_text                               pptx_shapes::set_text(zip, slides, op)
    add_textbox, add_shape                 pptx_shapes::add_textbox_or_shape(zip, slides, op)
    delete_shape                           pptx_shapes::delete_shape(zip, slides, op)
    add_table                              pptx_shapes::add_table(zip, slides, op)
    add_image                              pptx_shapes::add_image(proof, zip, slides, op)
    fit_text                               pptx_shapes::fit_text(measurer, zip, slides, op)
    set_table_cell_style                   pptx_shapes::set_table_cell_style(zip, slides, op)
    set_table_data, replace_image          pptx_shapes::set_table_data_or_replace_image(proof, zip, slides, op)
    group_shapes, ungroup_shape            pptx_shapes::group_shapes_or_ungroup_shape(zip, slides, op)
    add_media                              pptx_shapes::add_media(proof, zip, slides, op)
    crop_image                             pptx_shapes::crop_image(zip, slides, op)
    add_animation                          pptx_shapes::add_animation(zip, slides, op)
    set_shape                              pptx_shapes::set_shape(zip, slides, op)

`proof` is a `ReadProof` (the files an operation names are read through it); `measurer` is a
`text_metrics::TextMeasurer` over a font registry (the provisioned Office faces registered by the caller), the only thing
`fit_text` needs from the machine.

## Not compiled

The module and its tests were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead): the first build, `cargo test -p
mixdog-ooxml` (unit tests in src/pptx_shapes.rs and tests/twin_pptx_shapes.rs), is the check. The twin test replays
native/core/fixtures/office-pptx-shapes and needs no Node; `twin_live_pptx_shapes` (ignored) re-records through Node
(`--tree` must hold node_modules for @napi-rs/canvas).
